cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Aegis-40 soluble-boron-free integral PWR — OpenMC core model, scripts
  and neutronics results
message: >-
  If you use this model, these scripts or these results, please cite both
  the software (this file) and the associated article once published.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Achilova
    given-names: Samira
    affiliation: New Uzbekistan University, Tashkent, Uzbekistan
    email: s.achilova@newuu.uz
  - family-names: Ismailov
    given-names: Laziz
    affiliation: New Uzbekistan University, Tashkent, Uzbekistan
  - family-names: Abdikarimov
    given-names: Adilbek
    affiliation: New Uzbekistan University, Tashkent, Uzbekistan
repository-code: 'https://github.com/aegis-40/OpenMC'
abstract: >-
  Continuous-energy Monte Carlo model (OpenMC 0.15.3, ENDF/B-VIII.0) of a
  125 MWth, 37-assembly, 17x17, 2.0 m active-height natural-circulation
  soluble-boron-free integral PWR with in-vessel control-rod drives,
  together with the run scripts and complete result files behind the study
  "Relaxing the rod-ejection constraint in soluble-boron-free PWR cores:
  attainable control-rod worth and residual boron dependency with in-vessel
  drives". The model is fully three-dimensional and explicit at pin level
  across all 37 assemblies; no assembly homogenisation or few-group
  condensation is used at any stage. Results cover a complete 2x2 rod-worth
  matrix over absorber B-10 enrichment and cluster count, single-cluster
  worth resolved by symmetry class, a directly computed effective
  delayed-neutron fraction, the quasi-static reactivity response along a
  prescribed cooldown path, and the residual emergency-boron requirement
  for cold shutdown with the most reactive cluster stuck.
keywords:
  - soluble-boron-free
  - small modular reactor
  - integral PWR
  - control-rod worth
  - rod-ejection accident
  - shutdown margin
  - effective delayed neutron fraction
  - Monte Carlo
  - OpenMC
  - reactor physics
